CHAPTER 3 Remote Repository : SUMMARY

There is two type of repositories

-Local : reside on the computers of team members

-Remote: reside on a server accessible to everyone in the team, it's mainly used  to share data

Most version control work happens in the local repository

Features :

They both have branches, commits and tags but the local repository includes a working copy associated with it and the remote repository only consists of the bare ".git" repository folder

Usage 

The actual work on the project happens in the local repository, modifications are made and committed over there

The remote repository is only thought as a means for sharing and exchanging code between developers(not for actually working)

We can create a remote repository by cloning a local one using the --bare option or by using git init --bare on the command line
